A||N||8||Wrench||K&N Filter||||1
Z||000000||Wrench||09-27-1999||09:15 PM||||Anyone have any experience with the K&N air filters. I have an '86 GT and am considering a K&N filter. They claim more Horsepower but I really wonder. Looks like a good filter and the lifetime guarantee isn't bad, but more horsepower? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||SpeedPhreak||09-27-1999||09:24 PM||||the k&n filter is supposed to let a lot more air in the mix.  i dont have one on my fiero yet but i had one on my previous bike.  & i felt a small difference.  besides its resuable & i know people that swear by them.||||reg||6
Z||000002||sluppy123||09-27-1999||09:41 PM||||I have K&N air filter's on both my fieros (85' 2m4 & 87' GT) I didn't notice any differance in HP, but i did notice an increase in intake noise, the I-4 has a fast clicking noise and the V-6 has a really cool hissing sound above 2500 RPM. <P>I think they are worth buying, you do need to get a re-charge kit to clean them, but I shouldn't have to buy a new air filter for another MILLION miles:~}||||reg||14
Z||000003||WGraffiKs||09-27-1999||09:44 PM||||I've had a K&N on my 86.5 for years now.  I like it primarily for the better intake sound and cleanability, but acknowledged performance gains?  Questionable!  Go to <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/NitrousV6/Adams1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/NitrousV6/Adams1.html</A>   and read the section called "Things to leave alone"  or something like that.  Intake mods are best made along with other mods to complement them, I believe.  You may want to consider additional mods to enhance the performance promise of the K&N.<p>[This message has been edited by WGraffiKs (edited 09-27-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||TOM||09-28-1999||12:53 AM||||I have a K&N. I did it with some other mods as well and did notice a gain in power and in mileage.||||reg||1
Z||000005||BlackGT||09-28-1999||03:18 PM||||What other mods have you done to your Fiero and which one do you have?||||reg||6
